# Cursor IDE Rules — AI Software Engineering Framework
- Universal Entrypoint: Always read `AI_ENTRYPOINT.md` to identify the active lifecycle stage.
- Anti-Hallucination: Verify every file on disk before editing. Never guess imports or function signatures.
- Evidence Before Claims: Execute verification commands before claiming a task or bug fix is complete.
- Surgical Changes: Limit edits to the active task contract. Bug fixes must be <= 25 lines.
- Full Output: Never generate placeholder comments (`// ... existing code ...`).
- Release Gate: No code is marked production-ready until `node bin/asef.js gate-check .` reports 100/100.
